/-! # Scaffold for `import-shake.yml`: Mathlib without the tactic-extension cover

Temporary. Where a proof calls `norm_num`, `positivity` or `simp`, Lean records every module whose
extension the tactic consulted, and `lake shake` keeps them all: about forty modules (number theory,
combinatorics, `Sheaves.Init`, the specialised `norm_num` extensions) that no MathFin proof uses.
Importing Mathlib *without* those modules, and everything that imports them, takes them out of
the record, so shake replaces this import by what each file really uses. The workflow deletes this
file after the shake; nothing may import it on `main`.
-/
